# Agent PR cycle (lean)

**Cursor agent sessions only.** If running under Hermes, skip this file:
Hermes has its own models and does not have Bugbot or Security Review. Do
not require Composer/Grok slugs, Bugbot, or Security Review there. Hermes
keeps CI + its own luna/standard-development gates.

Autonomous create → review → merge. Do not wait on human review. Hard CI
failures, Luna NO_GO, and Bugbot findings still block.

## Implement (non-fast)

| Work | Who | Task slug |
|---|---|---|
| Easy / mechanical (flags, docs, tests, nits) | Composer 2.5 | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| Hard (contracts, schedulers, harness, extractors) | Grok 4.6 high | `cursor-grok-4.6-high` |

Do not use `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` (or other `*-fast` Grok) as the
implementer. Luna: `Task` tool, `model: gpt-5.6-luna-medium`,
`generalPurpose`, branch changes vs the default base. Never Opus-high.

## Non-trivial vs trivial

**Trivial** (skip Luna / Bugbot / Security; merge after CI green):

- Docs-only typos, badge/link/metadata, single-line comment, pure
  formatting with no logic change
- Housekeeping like license badge, topics, changelog date bumps

**Non-trivial** (Luna **and** Bugbot required):

- Any new/changed logic, scripts, compilers, extractors, tests, CI
  workflows, schemas, or generated security/report artifacts
- Multi-file features, refactors, or anything touching regexproof
  runtime / harness / batch / rule_diff

If unsure, treat as non-trivial. A comment or formatting edit that
changes CI/config/process semantics is non-trivial.

**Non-nit push** (re-run trigger): any push that would be non-trivial as
its own PR. Skip re-review for trivial pushes only.

## One question per reviewer

| Question | Who | When |
|---|---|---|
| Is the design/contract correct? | Luna | Every **non-trivial** PR |
| Is there a bug? | Bugbot | Every **non-trivial** PR, **after** Luna |
| Trust-boundary hole? | Security Review | Only if the diff touches clone URL, PAT, `subprocess`, `eval`, probe walker, or fail-open `except` |
| Second brain on Composer work? | Grok | Only if Luna returns NO_GO / CONFIRMED on a **contract** |

**Never:** Grok reviewing its own patch. Luna and Grok in parallel on
“is this correct?”. Grok on Composer argparse / docs / mechanical flags.
Security on diffs with no trust-boundary surface.

## Sequence

CI, Luna, and Bugbot must be green on the **same head** that becomes Ready
(and that later merges, except trivial nits on top of that head).

1. Implement on a branch. Open a **draft** PR (`gh pr create --draft`).
2. Wait for **CI green on this head** (or fix first). Presence, not just
   green — see **This repo — CI presence** below.
3. While draft: **Luna** (`Task`, `model: gpt-5.6-luna-medium`,
   `generalPurpose`, branch vs default base), then **Bugbot**
   (`review-bugbot`, `Diff: branch changes`). Escalate Grok / Security
   only per the table. Fix Luna **and** Bugbot CONFIRMED findings (or
   document FOLD / DISMISS) before Ready. Stay draft.
4. **Non-nit push** → wait for **CI green**, then Luna + Bugbot on the
   new head (Security only if a trust-boundary file changed). Trivial
   push → skip.
5. **`gh pr ready` only when CI + Luna + Bugbot are clean on this head**
   (and Security if it ran). Do not leave a finished PR in draft —
   CodeRabbit auto-review skips drafts.
6. Wait for `coderabbitai[bot]` `COMMENTED` on that SHA. A rate-limit
   comment is not a review. One fix push per round: Composer for nits,
   Grok only if a comment hits a contract. Wait out the round; do not
   push mid-review. Protocol: `docs/CODERABBIT.md`.
7. After CodeRabbit: one fix push per round. **Non-nit** → wait for
   **CI green**, then Luna + Bugbot (Security only if a trust-boundary
   file changed), then **back to step 6** (wait `COMMENTED` on the new
   SHA). **Trivial** nits/docs → skip Luna/Bugbot; still wait out the
   CodeRabbit round (step 6). CI must succeed on the merge head. Triage
   comments CONFIRMED / DISMISS / FOLD; do not auto-apply bot patches;
   human `REQUEST_CHANGES` outranks bots.
8. Merge (`gh pr merge`, usual strategy) only when **CI is green on the
   merge head**, Luna + Bugbot are clean on this head **or** on the last
   non-nit head if only trivial nits followed (and Security if it ran),
   and step 6 completed: CodeRabbit `COMMENTED` on the Ready SHA (or the
   latest fix-round SHA) with CONFIRMED comments triaged. Do not merge
   after Ready with no CodeRabbit round, or while a round is in flight.
   Next item.

Do not merge a non-trivial PR that is still draft, or with Luna NO_GO,
unresolved Luna or Bugbot CONFIRMED, a skipped/in-flight CodeRabbit
round, or un-triaged CodeRabbit CONFIRMED.
Do not merge on stale Luna / Bugbot from a **non-nit** head older than
the one you are merging (trivial nits on top of a reviewed head are fine).

## This repo — CI presence

Required verify jobs must **appear and succeed** on the merge head
(`gh pr checks`). A CodeQL-only rollup is not green (#205):

- `Z3 proof harness`
- `Golden suite (Python 3.12)` / `Golden suite (Python 3.13)`
- `Link check`
- `ReDoS stage (isolated)`
- `Read Python matrix`
- `Noodler backend (pinned asset + pre-flight, #220)` — job `name` must
  be YAML-quoted
